<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Leap Forward</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1958–1962</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Leap Forward was a campaign launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> in 1958 to turn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> rapidly into an industrial and communist society. Peasants were organised into vast people's communes, labour was diverted to backyard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> furnaces, and officials reported inflated harvests while grain was requisitioned. The resulting famine of 1959–61 killed an estimated 15 to 45 million people, and the campaign was abandoned by 1962.</p></div>
